description:
Company Background

 Our client provides shared services in analytics, technology, legal, accounting, and HR, supporting companies that deliver subscription-based financial research and educational products to millions of investors worldwide. The mission is to empower client companies with systems, support, and insights needed to deliver best-in-class financial intelligence products. The team operates in an integrated environment using Kanban methodology.

 Project Description

 The project focuses on developing and maintaining cloud-native services for a digital marketing platform within the financial information and software industry. The solution is built primarily with Java, Spring Boot, and AWS, with integrations into Salesforce. The engineer will contribute to backend development, serverless architecture, and the improvement of existing services.

 Technologies


 Java 17, Spring Boot 3.x

 AWS (Lambda, Step Functions, API Gateway, EKS, SQS, DynamoDB, RDS, S3, Kinesis)

 Kubernetes

 REST API, JPA, JUnit

 SQL (MySQL, PostgreSQL), NoSQL

 Event-driven architecture


 What You'll Do


 Analyze business requirements and translate them into smaller components of a serverless architecture;

 Design, develop, test, deploy, and maintain scalable and reliable backend services and REST APIs using Java, Spring Boot, and AWS;

 Collaborate with software engineers and product owners on solution design, task estimation, and technical decisions;

 Contribute to the improvement of software development processes and CI pipelines through Agile practices and sprint retrospectives;

 Communicate directly with the client's technical lead and other teams to clarify requirements, discuss technical solutions, and provide project updates;


 Job Requirements


 2+ years of professional software development experience with Java;

 Experience with Spring Framework, including Core, Data Access, Web, and Testing;

 Experience working with AWS services;

 Experience developing REST APIs and working with JPA;

 Experience with SQL (MySQL or PostgreSQL) and NoSQL databases;

 Solid understanding of OOP principles, SOLID, design patterns, data structures, and algorithms;

 Ability to write clean, maintainable code and unit tests using JUnit;

 Willingness to learn new technologies and complete Salesforce training;

 English level B2 (Upper-Intermediate) or higher;


 Nice to Have 


 Bachelor's degree in Computer Science or a related field;

 Familiarity with Node.js, TypeScript, or Angular;

 Experience with Salesforce technologies;


 What Do We Offer

 The global benefits package includes:


 Technical and non-technical training for professional and personal growth;

 Internal conferences and meetups to learn from industry experts;

 Support and mentorship from an experienced employee to help you professional grow and development;

 Health insurance;

 Sports activities to promote a healthy lifestyle;

 Flexible work options, including remote and hybrid opportunities;

 Referral program for bringing in new talent;

 Work anniversary program and additional vacation days.
